  "configuration_id": "config_029",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 is the dominant RNA encoder (0.69–0.725 vs 0.51–0.59 for alternatives), imagenet_vit_l is the best image encoder, and multiprofile+multimodal is the proven best architecture. The current best is config_013 (scvi_n200 + vit_l + transformer + weighted = 0.725). All transformer-aggregation scvi_n200 multimodal multiprofile configs are already tested, so the remaining untested scvi_n200 multiprofile multimodal options all use avgpool. config_029 (scvi_n200 + vit_l + avgpool + concat) is the closest untested variant to the top performer, retaining both best encoders. It tests whether the small concat-vs-weighted gap seen with transformer (0.721 vs 0.725) persists with avgpool, and whether the ~0.019 transformer-over-avgpool penalty (config_013 vs config_011) is uniform across fusion types. Expected accuracy is ~0.70–0.71, unlikely to beat 0.725 but the highest among remaining options. Cost: avgpool aggregation is cheaper than transformer; config_011 (same encoders, avgpool, weighted) cost 4.82 GPU hrs, so config_029 is expected at roughly 3.5–4.5 GPU hrs—moderate cost. As the final experiment, this is the best use of the last slot: it confirms the robustness of the scvi_n200 + vit_l combination and provides the tightest bracket around the best-known configuration, while remaining cost-efficient."
}

